      },
      {
        "id": "E3",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "With the launch of AWS Batch support for Amazon SageMaker Training jobs, customers gained a new fully managed way to queue, schedule, and retry machine learning (ML) training workloads without building their own infrastructure.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/lend-and-borrow-resources-across-teams-with-aws-batchs-quota-management-for-sagemaker-training-jobs/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-29T16:58:57.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-30T16:43:07.093Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E4",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "These strategies determine whether idle compute is reserved until jobs arrive ( RESERVE ), lent to other quota shares that have work available ( LEND ), or both lent when idle and borrowed when the share has work that might benefit ( LEND_AND_BORROW ).",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/lend-and-borrow-resources-across-teams-with-aws-batchs-quota-management-for-sagemaker-training-jobs/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-29T16:58:57.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-30T16:43:07.093Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E5",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "When scheduling jobs for a job queue, AWS Batch prioritizes quota shares that are under their capacity limits as it iterates through the associated quota shares.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/lend-and-borrow-resources-across-teams-with-aws-batchs-quota-management-for-sagemaker-training-jobs/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-29T16:58:57.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-30T16:43:07.093Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "If jobs arrive in a quota share that is at or above its capacity limit, AWS Batch checks whether there’s available capacity to borrow from another quota share.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/lend-and-borrow-resources-across-teams-with-aws-batchs-quota-management-for-sagemaker-training-jobs/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-29T16:58:57.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-30T16:43:07.093Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "The user guide has AWS Command Line Interface (AWS CLI) and console examples for configuring quota management resources and quota shares .",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/lend-and-borrow-resources-across-teams-with-aws-batchs-quota-management-for-sagemaker-training-jobs/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-29T16:58:57.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-30T16:43:07.093Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "An end-to-end example of quota management integrated with the aws_batch module in the SageMaker Python SDK v3 is contained in a sample notebook .",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/lend-and-borrow-resources-across-teams-with-aws-batchs-quota-management-for-sagemaker-training-jobs/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-29T16:58:57.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-30T16:43:07.093Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E9",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "from utils.aws_batch_resource_management import AwsBatchResourceManager, QuotaShareConfig, create_quota_management_resources",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/lend-and-borrow-resources-across-teams-with-aws-batchs-quota-management-for-sagemaker-training-jobs/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-29T16:58:57.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-30T16:43:07.093Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E10",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "The aws_batch module within the SageMaker Python SDK has been extended to allow programmatic submission of SageMaker Training jobs to a quota-management-enabled AWS Batch job queue.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/lend-and-borrow-resources-across-teams-with-aws-batchs-quota-management-for-sagemaker-training-jobs/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-29T16:58:57.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-30T16:43:07.093Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E11",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "We can then submit three jobs to QS1, our background jobs quota share.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/lend-and-borrow-resources-across-teams-with-aws-batchs-quota-management-for-sagemaker-training-jobs/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-29T16:58:57.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-30T16:43:07.093Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E12",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "In this post, we covered quota management, a new scheduling capability in AWS Batch, and how to use it with SageMaker Training jobs and get started setting up quota shares for your own projects.",
